 "gossip": {
  "text": "Rob and Darren, put the coffee down. Ravens tackle Ronnie Stanley has been ruled out with a toe injury, so Baltimore takes Lamar Jackson to Rio without him. The Maracan\u00e3 pitch is one that NFL and players' union field experts have spent days inspecting. When the union chief has to put out a lengthy statement about the grass, I'd call that a hazard, not a field. Zay Flowers is still questionable with a hamstring. Between you, you hold Baltimore in four bets. You're 60% in the two against Andy and 49% in the two against Steve. If I were you, I'd watch the first series through my fingers.\n\nAndy, don't get smug. Yesterday this column named Ben Bartch as one of four questionable Lions linemen. Today he's out, and safety Thomas Harper is out with him. Detroit is still only a 6.5-point favourite over the Jets, three points less than at the open. Both Ravens-versus-Lions bets now come down to whose offensive line is held together with more tape. I still take Baltimore, on the theory that Lamar can outrun a missing tackle and nobody on your side can.\n\nSteve is the favourite in all three of his bets. The Chiefs' title price has shortened, and Andy Reid gives rookie corner Mansoor Delane a \"good chance\" of playing in Miami. The line did slip from 10.5 to 10 today. Half a point is not a crisis. Steve's only real problem is that he has nothing to worry about, which is usually when this column starts watching him.",
  "written": "2026-09-26T06:16:32-07:00",
  "based_on": 23
 }
}